{"records":[{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"yrdmc8fw4j","title":"Uncropped Blots Related to Pathmanathan et al, B cell linker protein (BLNK) is a novel regulator of Met receptor signaling and trafficking in non-small cell lung cancer ","description":"Uncropped Blots related to Pathmanathan et al, B cell linker protein (BLNK) is a novel regulator of Met receptor signaling and trafficking in non-small cell lung cancer. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-11-04T19:53:55.915Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/yrdmc8fw4j","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/yrdmc8fw4j"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shivanthy","last_name":"Pat","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Cell Signaling","Receptor Tyrosine Kinase","Protein Interaction"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vyg3bysz6y","title":"Automated Multi-Label PET-CT ROI and NHOC metric pipeline","description":"Performed automated Multi-Label PET-CT ROI and NHOC metric pipeline for paper \"A novel 18F-FDG PET radiomics signature for non-small cell lung cancer prognostication\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-04T15:00:47.724Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vyg3bysz6y","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vyg3bysz6y"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mitch","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/00c489v88","name":"Academy of Medical Sciences","grant_id":"SGL026\\1024"},{"id":"https://ror.org/0187kwz08","name":"National Institute for Health Research","grant_id":"CL-2021-21-005"}],"categories":["Computer Program","Automated Segmentation","Radiomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nzrs6z3677","title":"Lung cancer cell derived exosomes enhance the metastasis of non-small cell lung cancer via SNHG12/miR-326/SLC7A11 axis","description":"The data are the raw data for the paper entitled \"Lung cancer cell derived exosomes enhance the metastasis of non-small cell lung cancer via SNHG12/miR-326/SLC7A11 axis\". ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-03-08T21:06:22.876Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nzrs6z3677","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nzrs6z3677"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rong","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Clinical Oncology","Experimental Oncology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fpnmx3f5tp","title":"Combined analysis of gut microbiome and serum metabolomics reveals novel biomarkers in patients with early-stage non-small cell lung cancer ","description":"early-stage non-small cell lung cancer serum metabolomics ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-12T13:35:16.013Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fpnmx3f5tp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fpnmx3f5tp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Boxiong","last_name":"Ni","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mmnwww6n3s","title":"LZTFL1 Rewires NADPH–Glutathione Metabolism to Amplify Ferroptosis","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent form of regulated cell death, represents a therapeutic vulnerability in apoptosis-resistant cancers. Here, we identify leucine zipper transcription factor-like 1 (LZTFL1) as a key regulator of ferroptosis that rewires glutathione (GSH) metabolism. A genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 screen and multi-omics analysis revealed that LZTFL1 promotes oxidation of glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD), limiting NADPH production and GSH regeneration. GSH depletion in turn enhanced LZTFL1 translation via an AKT–mTOR–eIF4E pathway, establishing a feed-forward loop that amplifies ferroptosis. In vivo, the LZTFL1–FHOD1–G6PD axis sensitized xenograft and patient-derived xenograft models to ferroptosis, correlating with lipid peroxidation, reduced GSH, and extended survival. Clinically, LZTFL1 expression restored cisplatin efficacy in resistant lung and ovarian cancer cells and predicted better survival outcomes in LUAD patients. Moreover, FDA-approved compounds upregulated LZTFL1 and re-sensitized resistant tumors to cisplatin. These findings define LZTFL1 as both a biomarker and therapeutic target for enhancing ferroptosis-based cancer therapy. The files below contain raw western blot images and flow cytometry data from this study.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-12T06:59:22.445Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mmnwww6n3s","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mmnwww6n3s"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"XIANGFEI","last_name":"XUE","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot","Flowmetry"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jr8ds894bf","title":"Data for: Identification of CALB1 as a Driver of Aggressive Tumorigenesis and Chemoresistance in Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer","description":"This dataset contains the original and analyzed data supporting the research findings of the study entitled \"Identification of CALB1 as a Driver of Aggressive Tumorigenesis and Chemoresistance in Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-30T16:26:08.856Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jr8ds894bf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jr8ds894bf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"feng","last_name":"Mao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f5jtt3s8hv","title":"GCN2 is a determinant of the response to WEE1 kinase inhibition in small-cell lung cancer ","description":"Patients with small-cell lung cancer (SCLC) are in dire need of more effective therapeutic options. Frequent disruption of the G1 checkpoint in SCLC cells creates a dependency on the G2/M checkpoint to maintain genomic integrity. Indeed, in pre-clinical models, inhibiting the G2/M checkpoint kinase WEE1 shows promise in inhibiting SCLC growth. However, toxicity and acquired resistance have limited the clinical effectiveness of this strategy. Here, using CRISPR/Cas9 knockout screens in vitro and in vivo, we identified multiple factors influencing the response of SCLC cells to the WEE1 kinase inhibitor AZD1775, including the GCN2 kinase and other members of its signaling pathway. Rapid activation of GCN2 upon AZD1775 treatment triggers a stress response in SCLC cells. Pharmacological or genetic activation of the GCN2 pathway enhances cancer cell killing by AZD1775. Thus, activation of the GCN2 pathway represents a novel approach for augmenting the efficacy of WEE1 inhibitors in SCLC.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-26T09:21:15.032Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f5jtt3s8hv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f5jtt3s8hv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alexander","last_name":"Drainas","orcid":"0000-0001-9081-9850"},{"first_name":"Julien","last_name":"Sage","orcid":"0000-0002-8928-9968"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Flow Cytometry","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":122378,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":144,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":122378,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":121825,"restricted":61,"embargoed":492},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2091},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":623},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":445},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":406},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":400},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":394},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":363},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":312},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":249},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":216}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":119800},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1899},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":177},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":119},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":74},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":65},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Uni